<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="about-intro">
            <div class="prose fade-in">
                <p>Elephas Consultancy is <strong>Leonard Hulley</strong>: a Microsoft-stack engineer who has spent more than 20 years building and integrating business systems, and has worked with Dynamics CRM and Dynamics 365 since 2013.</p>
                <p>He learned the trade in small businesses — writing property data feeds for estate agents, building a complete business system for a network of advertising screens largely on his own, and co-founding Infobox Media, a consultancy for direct clients and digital agencies. In 2013 a CRM programme at the Chartered Society of Physiotherapy brought him into Dynamics. From 2014 to 2017 he was at Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew, <a href="/case-studies/royal-botanic-gardens-kew/">recovering its ticketing and CRM programme</a> and then running its IT programme.</p>
                <p>Elephas began trading in the UK in 2014, became his full-time business when he moved to Sweden in 2017, and was incorporated as Elephas Consultancy AB in 2021. Since then the work has included National Highways, Southern Communications Group, Argyll, UK heritage attractions, and Microsoft partners in the UK and Sweden — <a href="/case-studies/">see the case studies</a>.</p>
                <p>When you hire Elephas, you talk directly to the person who builds. No sales layer, no juniors learning at your expense, no handovers where details go missing. What we do have is modern AI tooling that gives a single senior engineer the capacity of a team — <a href="/how-we-work/">read how that works</a>.</p>
                <p>The name? The elephant stands for memory, strength and patience — qualities we think belong in good software and long client relationships.</p>
            </div>
            <figure class="about-portrait fade-in">
                <img src="/images/leonard-hulley.jpg" alt="Leonard Hulley, founder of Elephas Consultancy" width="800" height="800">
